# What this repository does NOT track.
#
# Everything the code writes is regenerable from the inputs named in the README, so no
# output, cache or rendered figure is tracked. The rules are written by FORMAT and
# LOCATION rather than by the name of any particular run, so a new output file is ignored
# the day it first appears instead of the day someone remembers to add a line here.
#
# Six data files ARE tracked. Five are inputs: the profile HMM under dat/models/, the
# curated control set under dat/control_set/, and under dat/criteria/ the anchor targets
# step 4 checks its grid against together with the two files their cells were transcribed
# from. The sixth is a result: the control set's validation predictions, beside the control
# set. Every one of them that a rule below would catch is re-included by name.

# ---- generated tables and caches under dat/ ---------------------------------------
# dat/ is where every run lands. Ignore the tabular and cache formats wholesale; the
# shipped files are re-included underneath.
dat/**/*.csv
dat/**/*.tsv
dat/**/*.json
dat/**/*.jsonl
dat/**/*.txt
dat/**/*.jls
dat/**/*.log
dat/**/*.gz
dat/**/*.zip
dat/**/*.toml
!dat/control_set/known_cofactor_mdhs.tsv
# The classifier's call on each control of the shipped control set: a result, tracked as the
# record of that validation. No code reads it, and a validation run writes its own tables
# into a directory of its own (see below), never over this file.
!dat/control_set/control_validation_predictions.csv

# ---- the data root, when it lives inside the clone --------------------------------
# $LNFINDER_DATA defaults to dat/ in this clone, so an unpacked data set lands in the
# directories below (docs/DATA.md gives the layout, docs/data_manifest.sha256 its
# checksums). They are ignored whole rather than by format: the archive is large, several
# of its files are results, and a rule by format would let a new extension through.
dat/habitat/
dat/census/
dat/criteria/*
# The anchor targets and their two sources are tracked inputs, not tables a run produced:
# step 4 checks its grid against them, and that check is worth nothing if the file it reads
# is not in the history. dat/criteria/ is ignored by its contents rather than whole, because
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded; the deposited criteria
# file that lands beside them when the data set is unpacked in place stays ignored.
!dat/criteria/anchor_targets.csv
!dat/criteria/impl_4.csv
!dat/criteria/impl_w1.csv
dat/determinant/
dat/derived/
dat/structures/
dat/MANIFEST.sha256
# A taxonomy dump unpacked anywhere. Nothing tracked here carries this extension.
*.dmp

# ---- whole directories a run creates ----------------------------------------------
# No code in this release writes any of these three: a general response cache, the pocket
# export and the control-set validation harness all lack a command-line driver here. They
# are ignored anyway, so that a reader who calls those library functions on their own data,
# or who brings a driver of their own, does not commit the result by accident.
dat/cache/
dat/pockets_exported/
dat/control_set/validate_run*/

# Kept for older working trees, and for nothing else. The habitat relation cache (step 1)
# and the background scan's working directory (step 2) are written under the data root now —
# that is dat/habitat/, which the block above already ignores whole — so no code in this
# release writes either of these two paths. The rules stay so that a tree checked out before
# the data root existed does not start offering up a directory of stored response bodies, or
# a scan's HMMER working files, the day somebody pulls.
dat/omnicrobe_cache/
dat/background_scan/

# ---- a run that has not passed its gates leaves its output staged -----------------
# Each step names its own staging directory, and step 5's is _staging_habitat_figure, so
# the glob has to cover any name a step invents rather than the one name the first step
# happened to use.
_staging/
**/_staging*/

# ---- half-written and gate-failed siblings of an output, wherever they land --------
# Outputs are written to <name>.part and renamed into place, and a step whose acceptance
# checks fail leaves this run's table as <name>.pending and renames the table it would
# have replaced to <name>.stale. None of those names ends in the extension the rules
# above match, so they are matched here by suffix, format-globally. Nothing tracked in
# this repository carries any of these suffixes.
*.part
*.pending
*.stale

# ---- run outputs that land in a figure directory the user names --------------------
# The figure directory is whatever --figdir / $LNFINDER_FIGDIR points at, so it cannot be
# ignored by location. These are the names steps 4 and 5 publish, ignored wherever they
# land. Add -f only for something you have checked is not a result.
*_source_data.csv
*caption_values*.csv
*_provenance.csv
habitat_robustness.csv
habitat_sensitivity*.csv
habitat_sensitivity_table.md
# Steps 1 and 3 write these under dat/ by default, where the rules above already catch
# them; named here as well so that relocating a run with --calls / --stats / --summary
# cannot land a result table somewhere this file does not reach.
habitat_taxon_calls.csv
habitat_enrichment*.csv
habitat_arm_summary.csv

# ---- census output, wherever a census was told to land ----------------------------
# LNFINDER_CENSUS_OUT is yours to choose, and the tabular rules above are anchored to
# dat/. A manifest carries counts and local paths, so it is ignored by name everywhere.
*.manifest.toml
census_rebuild_*/

# ---- figures, logs and rendered output ---------------------------------------------
# figs/ is only the conventional figure directory; the pipeline's figure directory is
# whatever --figdir names, which is why the output NAMES are ignored above as well.
figs/
logs/
*.log
nohup.out

# ---- sequence, alignment, clustering and structure files, wherever they land -------
# None of these belongs in version control: they are large, they are regenerated by the
# external tools the README lists, and they are the inputs this repository does not carry.
*.afa
*.fa
*.fasta
*.faa
*.fna
*.sto
*.uc
*.pdb
*.cif
*.nwk
*.newick
*.tblout
*.domtblout

# ---- documents, archives and images -----------------------------------------------
# Rendered figures and working documents are the easiest thing to commit by accident, so
# they are ignored by extension everywhere. Anything that genuinely belongs in the
# repository can be added with `git add -f`.
*.pdf
*.docx
*.pptx
*.xlsx
*.odt
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.tif
*.tiff
*.bundle
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.7z

# ---- Julia -------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Manifest-v*.toml
*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.mem
*.cov
/docs/build/
/deps/deps.jl
/deps/build.log
LocalPreferences.toml

# ---- editor, OS and agent state -----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.claude/
*.local.md
*.local.toml
*.local.json

# ---- the environment figure's inputs ----------------------------------------------
# Three small tables (under 5 KB together) are tracked so scripts/fold_change_figure.jl
# renders from a bare clone with no data set to hand. They are DERIVED: scripts/
# prevalence.py and scripts/prevalence_phylum_average.py regenerate them byte-for-byte
# from <data root>/habitat/, which is how they were made. Everything else the figure
# step writes stays ignored by the dat/ rules above.
!dat/figure/prevalence.csv
!dat/figure/prevalence_phylum_average.csv
!dat/figure/thermal_options.csv
